Put “Do it again!” before the thunder and it’s a request. Put it just after the mistake and it’s permission. Put it at the end of the show and it’s an encore.

And it matters who says it. From the stage manager, it means reset the cue. From a kid in the front row, it tells the performer the mistake was fun. For a second, the kid gets to direct the show.

That’s where I’d look for positioning in Pantheon. Where does an idea land, who gets to say it, and what can somebody do with it right then?